{{ElectionsGA}}
The '''2018 United States House of Representatives elections in Georgia''' will be held on November 6, 2018, to elect the fourteen [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. Representatives]] from the [[U.S. state|state]] of [[Georgia (U.S. state)|Georgia]], one from each of the state's fourteen [[Georgia's congressional districts|congressional districts]]. The elections will coincide with a [[Georgia gubernatorial election, 2018|gubernatorial election]], as well as [[United States House of Representatives elections, 2018|other elections]] to the House of Representatives, [[United States Senate elections, 2018|elections]] to the [[United States Senate]] and various [[United States elections, 2018#State elections|state]] and [[United States elections, 2018#Local elections|local elections]]. The primary elections took place on May 22, 2018.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://ballotpedia.org/United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Georgia,_2018|title=United States House of Representatives elections in Georgia, 2018 - Ballotpedia|access-date=2018-02-20|language=en-US}}</ref>

If in any given congressional district no candidate gains a simple majority of the votes, a runoff election between the top two candidates within said congressional district will be held nine weeks later on January 8, 2019.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://sos.ga.gov/index.php/elections/2018_elections_and_voter_registration_calendar|title=2018 Elections and Voter Registration Calendar|access-date=2018-10-30|language=en-US}}</ref>

{{Toclimit|limit=2}}

